From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 03:55:38 +0800
Subject: rtc: pm8xxx: keep protected counters out of hctosys without an epoch

Keep relative alarms and suspend accounting available on PM8xxx
devices with a protected counter and no epoch offset. Exclude
that counter from the initial system wall-clock update.

Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/9c93f788af20a4cd686852626270a0fcf4cbe8fc
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
index e624f848c22b5799d23107518bbfd01b2e93d150..36fcb3908acc00ba6300c90cc1da14568dae6832 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-pm8xxx.c
@@ -639,6 +639,11 @@ static int pm8xxx_rtc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	rtc_dd->rtc->ops = &pm8xxx_rtc_ops;
 	rtc_dd->rtc->range_max = U32_MAX;
+	/* Without an epoch offset, the protected counter is only useful for
+	 * relative alarms and suspend accounting, not setting wall time.
+	 */
+	if (!rtc_dd->allow_set_time && !rtc_dd->offset)
+		set_bit(RTC_NO_HCTOSYS, &rtc_dd->rtc->flags);
 
 	if (rtc_dd->alarm_irq) {
 		rc = devm_request_any_context_irq(&pdev->dev, rtc_dd->alarm_irq,
